{% extends 'layouts/default.twig' %}

{% block content %}
<h1>Fridays after dark</h1>

<figure class="hero"><img src="/assets/market/hero.jpg" alt="A wall of glowing paper lanterns in orange, gold and teal"></figure>

<div>
	<p>Forty stalls, one brass band and a very long string of lights on Mill Street, every Friday from May to October.</p>
</div>

<p><a class="button" href="/events">See what's on</a></p>

<h2>What you'll find</h2>
<p>Street food the whole length of the Row: hand-pulled noodles, wood-fired pita, skewers, and dumplings until they run out. In between are the growers and makers, with bread, peppers, pottery, hot sauce and Ruth's knife sharpening by the crosswalk.</p>

<h2>Getting here</h2>
<p>Lantern Row is the 200 block of Mill Street, between the old feed store and the rail spur. Park in the lot behind the feed store, two minutes' walk away. Bring cash for the smaller stalls, and a bag.</p>
{% endblock %}
